  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (4-(Prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexyl)methanol and HaCaT through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is identified as a target in SNU-387, which is itself a target of two different compounds. One of these compounds, (3S,7R,8Ar)-3-Benzyl-7-Hydroxyhexahydropyrrolo[1,2-A]Pyrazine-1,4-Dione, directly targets HaCaT. Another compound, VMRC-LCP, is also a target of (4-(Prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexyl)methanol, which in turn targets (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, which also targets HaCaT. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may influence HaCaT through various molecular mechanisms, possibly involving signaling pathways or metabolic processes. The evidence is consistent across different targets, suggesting a broader biological relevance, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
